        "$a_n = \\frac{2}{\\pi}\\int_0^{\\pi} x^2 \\cos(nx) dx = \\frac{4(-1)^n}{n^2}$.",
        "En $x = \\pi$ : $\\pi^2 = \\frac{\\pi^2}{3} + 4\\sum_{n=1}^{+\\infty} \\frac{(-1)^n(-1)^n}{n^2} = \\frac{\\pi^2}{3} + 4\\sum \\frac{1}{n^2}$.",
        "Donc $\\sum \\frac{1}{n^2} = \\frac{\\pi^2 - \\pi^2/3}{4} = \\frac{\\pi^2}{6}$."
